IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-reading`

-- Tests for il-interpretation-reading.l4 (Law ss 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 25).
-- Expected values were decided from the words of each section before the module was run. A failing assertion is a
-- finding: none was edited to match the code. In this file the matter is either one that nothing displaces
-- (`a matter nothing displaces`, `a matter another provision deals with`, `a matter whose context is inconsistent
-- with the Law` are defined in il-interpretation-gate.l4) or one of the two that s 1 displaces.

§ `Tests: the rules of reading`

§§ `s 2: a defined term bears its definition`

`a use in the defining enactment` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in the enactment that defines it`
    `the form it takes` IS `the term itself`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS FALSE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS FALSE

`a use in regulations made under the defining enactment` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in regulations made under the enactment that defines it`
    `the form it takes` IS `the term itself`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS FALSE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS FALSE

`a use in some other enactment` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in some other enactment`
    `the form it takes` IS `the term itself`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS FALSE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS FALSE

`a derived form used in the defining enactment` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in the enactment that defines it`
    `the form it takes` IS `a grammatical form derived from the term`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS FALSE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS FALSE

`a derived form used in regulations made under the defining enactment` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in regulations made under the enactment that defines it`
    `the form it takes` IS `a grammatical form derived from the term`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS FALSE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS FALSE

`a derived form used in some other enactment` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in some other enactment`
    `the form it takes` IS `a grammatical form derived from the term`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS FALSE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS FALSE

`a use where another provision deals with the matter` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in the enactment that defines it`
    `the form it takes` IS `the term itself`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS TRUE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS FALSE

`a use inconsistent with the definition` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH
    `where it is used` IS `in the enactment that defines it`
    `the form it takes` IS `the term itself`
    `another provision deals with the matter` IS FALSE
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS TRUE

-- tests: L2
#ASSERT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a use in the defining enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a use in regulations made under the defining enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a use in some other enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a derived form used in the defining enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a derived form used in regulations made under the defining enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a derived form used in some other enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a use where another provision deals with the matter` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a use inconsistent with the definition` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
-- s 2 is itself subject to s 1: where s 1 displaces the Law, s 2 does not say what the term means.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a use in the defining enactment` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` `a use in the defining enactment` `, for` `a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"

§§ `s 4: a person includes a body of persons`

#ASSERT `s 4 — a reference to a person reaches` `a natural person` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 4 — a reference to a person reaches` `a corporation` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 4 — a reference to a person reaches` `a body of persons that is not a corporation` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 4 — a reference to a person reaches` `a thing that is neither a person nor a body of persons` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 4 — a reference to a person reaches` `a corporation` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

§§ `s 5: singular and plural, both ways`

#ASSERT `s 5 — what is said in` `the singular` `reaches` `the plural` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 5 — what is said in` `the plural` `reaches` `the singular` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 5 — what is said in` `the singular` `reaches` `the singular` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 5 — what is said in` `the plural` `reaches` `the plural` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5 — what is said in` `the singular` `reaches` `the plural` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5 — what is said in` `the plural` `reaches` `the singular` `, for` `a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law`

§§ `s 6: masculine and feminine, both ways`

#ASSERT `s 6 — what is said in` `the masculine` `reaches` `the feminine` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 6 — what is said in` `the feminine` `reaches` `the masculine` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 6 — what is said in` `the masculine` `reaches` `the masculine` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 6 — what is said in` `the feminine` `reaches` `the feminine` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 6 — what is said in` `the masculine` `reaches` `the feminine` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

§§ `s 7: "or" and "other" do not infer from the list`

`the word "or" alone` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS TRUE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS FALSE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`the word "other" with "similar"` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS TRUE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS TRUE
    `it is "or"` IS FALSE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`a word that is not "or" or "other", with an analogy word` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS TRUE
    `it is "or"` IS FALSE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`a word that is not "or" or "other", with no analogy word` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS FALSE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`the word or named by its own field` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS TRUE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`the word other named by its own field` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS FALSE
    `it is "other"` IS TRUE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`an expression like them named by its own field` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS FALSE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS TRUE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`the word or with similar named by its own field` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS TRUE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS TRUE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`the word or with of like kind named by its own field` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS TRUE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS TRUE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

`the word or with another expression of analogy named by its own field` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS TRUE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS TRUE

`a word of none of those kinds` MEANS `A general word that follows a list` WITH
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy` IS FALSE
    `it is "or"` IS FALSE
    `it is "other"` IS FALSE
    `it is an expression like them` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "similar"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"` IS FALSE
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy` IS FALSE

-- tests: L7
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `the word "or" alone` EQUALS `apart from the list: it does not take its sense from the list`
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `the word "other" with "similar"` EQUALS `by analogy to the list`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `a word that is not "or" or "other", with an analogy word` BECAUSE "s 7 speaks only of the words \"or\" and \"other\" and expressions like them"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `a word that is not "or" or "other", with no analogy word` BECAUSE "s 7 speaks only of the words \"or\" and \"other\" and expressions like them"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter another provision deals with` `:` `the word "or" alone`
-- Each word and each sign of analogy the section names is a field of its own beside the phrase as printed.
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `the word or named by its own field` EQUALS `apart from the list: it does not take its sense from the list`
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `the word other named by its own field` EQUALS `apart from the list: it does not take its sense from the list`
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `an expression like them named by its own field` EQUALS `apart from the list: it does not take its sense from the list`
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `the word or with similar named by its own field` EQUALS `by analogy to the list`
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `the word or with of like kind named by its own field` EQUALS `by analogy to the list`
#ASSERT `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `the word or with another expression of analogy named by its own field` EQUALS `by analogy to the list`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `a word of none of those kinds` BECAUSE "s 7 speaks only of the words \"or\" and \"other\" and expressions like them"

§§ `s 9: "according to"`

`"according to" the enactment itself` MEANS `A use of "according to"` WITH
    `the expression is "according to" or one like it` IS TRUE
    `what the act is done according to` IS `the enactment itself`

`"according to" regulations made under the enactment` MEANS `A use of "according to"` WITH
    `the expression is "according to" or one like it` IS TRUE
    `what the act is done according to` IS `regulations made under the enactment`

`"according to" some other instrument` MEANS `A use of "according to"` WITH
    `the expression is "according to" or one like it` IS TRUE
    `what the act is done according to` IS `some other instrument`

`some other expression, regulations made under the enactment` MEANS `A use of "according to"` WITH
    `the expression is "according to" or one like it` IS FALSE
    `what the act is done according to` IS `regulations made under the enactment`

-- tests: L9
#ASSERT `s 9 — "according to" an enactment reaches an act done according to` `"according to" the enactment itself` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 9 — "according to" an enactment reaches an act done according to` `"according to" regulations made under the enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9 — "according to" an enactment reaches an act done according to` `"according to" some other instrument` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9 — "according to" an enactment reaches an act done according to` `some other expression, regulations made under the enactment` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 9 — "according to" an enactment reaches an act done according to` `"according to" regulations made under the enactment` `, for` `a matter another provision deals with`

§§ `s 25: a reference to an enactment`

`the 2000 wording` MEANS `A version of an enactment's wording` WITH `in force from` IS YMD 2000 1 1, `wording` IS "the wording as first enacted"
`the 2010 wording` MEANS `A version of an enactment's wording` WITH `in force from` IS YMD 2010 1 1, `wording` IS "the wording with an added provision"

GIVETH A LIST OF `A version of an enactment's wording`
`no versions` MEANS EMPTY

`an enactment amended once and not replaced` MEANS `An enactment that another enactment refers to` WITH
    `its versions` IS LIST `the 2000 wording`, `the 2010 wording`
    `provisions of another enactment took its place from` IS NOTHING

`an enactment amended once and replaced from 2020-06-01` MEANS `An enactment that another enactment refers to` WITH
    `its versions` IS LIST `the 2000 wording`, `the 2010 wording`
    `provisions of another enactment took its place from` IS JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)

-- tests: L25
-- The wording in force on the day it is resorted to, on both sides of the day the amendment took effect.
#ASSERT `s 25 — the wording in force on` (YMD 2005 1 1) `among` (LIST `the 2000 wording`, `the 2010 wording`) EQUALS JUST `the 2000 wording`
#ASSERT `s 25 — the wording in force on` (YMD 2009 12 31) `among` (LIST `the 2000 wording`, `the 2010 wording`) EQUALS JUST `the 2000 wording`
#ASSERT `s 25 — the wording in force on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `among` (LIST `the 2000 wording`, `the 2010 wording`) EQUALS JUST `the 2010 wording`
#ASSERT `s 25 — the wording in force on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `among` (LIST `the 2000 wording`, `the 2010 wording`) EQUALS JUST `the 2010 wording`
#ASSERT `s 25 — the wording in force on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `among` (LIST `the 2010 wording`, `the 2000 wording`) EQUALS JUST `the 2010 wording`
#ASSERT `s 25 — the wording in force on` (YMD 1999 12 31) `among` (LIST `the 2000 wording`, `the 2010 wording`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25 — the wording in force on` (YMD 2005 1 1) `among` `no versions` EQUALS NOTHING
-- What a reference reaches: the wording in force, and the provisions that came in its place.
#ASSERT (`s 25 — what a reference to an enactment reaches when it is resorted to on` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `an enactment amended once and not replaced`)'s `the wording in force on the day it is resorted to` EQUALS JUST `the 2010 wording`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25 — what a reference to an enactment reaches when it is resorted to on` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `an enactment amended once and not replaced`)'s `the provisions that came in its place in another enactment`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25 — what a reference to an enactment reaches when it is resorted to on` (YMD 2020 5 31) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `an enactment amended once and replaced from 2020-06-01`)'s `the provisions that came in its place in another enactment`
#ASSERT (`s 25 — what a reference to an enactment reaches when it is resorted to on` (YMD 2020 6 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `an enactment amended once and replaced from 2020-06-01`)'s `the provisions that came in its place in another enactment`
#ASSERT (`s 25 — what a reference to an enactment reaches when it is resorted to on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` `:` `an enactment amended once and replaced from 2020-06-01`)'s `the provisions that came in its place in another enactment`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25 — what a reference to an enactment reaches when it is resorted to on` (YMD 2015 1 1) `, for` `a matter another provision deals with` `:` `an enactment amended once and not replaced`

