-- On the day the Law commenced, and the day before it, section 8 reaches an enactment either way (the date does not matter).
#ASSERT `s 1 — section` 8 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 1981 10 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 1 — section` 8 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 1981 9 30) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
-- Section 3: for an enactment given after the Law every word; for an earlier one only sin, misdemeanour and felony, so the answer turns on the word.
#ASSERT `s 1 — section` 3 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 1990 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT `s 1 — section` 3 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an administrative direction` `given on` (YMD 1990 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — section` 3 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is a private contract` `given on` (YMD 1990 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 3 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 3 reaches the words of an enactment given before the Law only for sin, misdemeanour and felony; for every other word the Ordinance's definitions continue to govern, so the answer turns on the word"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 3 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 1981 10 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "a day-level date cannot say whether an enactment given on the day the Law commenced was given before 00:01 on that day"
-- The other sections of the Law are not rules that s 1 applies.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 1 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26 to enactments and administrative directions; sections 1 and 27 to 33 say how the Law applies, what it repeals and where its text was merged, and are not rules that s 1 applies"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 27 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26 to enactments and administrative directions; sections 1 and 27 to 33 say how the Law applies, what it repeals and where its text was merged, and are not rules that s 1 applies"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 31 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26 to enactments and administrative directions; sections 1 and 27 to 33 say how the Law applies, what it repeals and where its text was merged, and are not rules that s 1 applies"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 33 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26 to enactments and administrative directions; sections 1 and 27 to 33 say how the Law applies, what it repeals and where its text was merged, and are not rules that s 1 applies"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 0 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26 to enactments and administrative directions; sections 1 and 27 to 33 say how the Law applies, what it repeals and where its text was merged, and are not rules that s 1 applies"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 34 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 1 applies the rules of interpretation of sections 2 to 26 to enactments and administrative directions; sections 1 and 27 to 33 say how the Law applies, what it repeals and where its text was merged, and are not rules that s 1 applies"
-- The gate still applies.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 8 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter another provision deals with` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section` 8 `of the Law reaches an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `given on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, for` `a matter whose context is inconsistent with the Law` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"

§§ `s 25: the kind of instrument that makes the reference`

-- tests: L25
-- s 25 speaks of a reference to an enactment in another enactment. A reference in a private contract or any other document is not within it;
-- whether one in an administrative direction is within it the sources do not say, so the rule refuses (F37).
#ASSERT `s 25 — a reference to an enactment made in an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `is within s 25, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25 — a reference to an enactment made in an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is a private contract` `is within s 25, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25 — a reference to an enactment made in an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is some other document` `is within s 25, for` `a matter nothing displaces`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25 — a reference to an enactment made in an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an administrative direction` `is within s 25, for` `a matter nothing displaces` BECAUSE "s 25 speaks of a reference to an enactment in another enactment; s 1 applies the Law to administrative directions, but nothing says whether a reference made in an administrative direction is within s 25"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25 — a reference to an enactment made in an instrument of the kind` `the instrument is an enactment` `is within s 25, for` `a matter another provision deals with` BECAUSE "the Law is displaced here: another provision deals with the matter, or the matter or its context is inconsistent with the Law, so the Law does not say what the words mean"
